From: RaikaShinohara <321751277+RaikaShinohara@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: max77693-haptic - enable the motor bias on MAX77705

The MAX77705 has the MAX77843 motor bias bit (MAINCTRL1 bit 7, register
0x02 on the PMIC) and the motor does not move without it. Samsung sets
it at probe (max77705_vibrator.c, max77705_vibrator_init_reg()).

---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c
@@ -88,7 +88,13 @@
 {
 	int error;
 
-	if (haptic->dev_type != TYPE_MAX77843)
+	/*
+	 * The MAX77705 has the same motor bias bit at the same address
+	 * (MAINCTRL1 0x02, bit 7); Samsung's driver sets it before driving
+	 * the motor, which does not move without it.
+	 */
+	if (haptic->dev_type != TYPE_MAX77843 &&
+	    haptic->dev_type != TYPE_MAX77705)
 		return 0;
 
 	error = regmap_update_bits(haptic->regmap_haptic,
